{"uid":"b60f2c584d0282e6","name":"test_validating_a_finding_emits_one_warning_naming_the_extra_key","fullName":"tests.test_structured_findings#test_validating_a_finding_emits_one_warning_naming_the_extra_key","historyId":"8b6f29665742d53a1d9c84cae61167e7","time":{"start":1792072027963,"stop":1792072027963,"duration":0},"description":"Task 014 (requirement E.1, #190): the warning is emitted BY\n    VALIDATION, not only available from `finding_warnings` on request --\n    a caller that merely validates an otherwise-valid finding carrying one\n    unrecognised key gets EXACTLY ONE `UnrecognisedFindingFieldWarning`\n    naming that key, and no validation error. Exactly one means one\n    emission in total, not one per channel: an earlier revision of this\n    module ALSO logged the same text through a module logger, so a single\n    unrecognised key was named twice (two stderr lines). This asserts the\n    one stdlib-`warnings` emission and that nothing anywhere in the\n    logging tree logs a duplicate of it at WARNING or above.","descriptionHtml":"<p>Task 014 (requirement E.1, #190): the warning is emitted BY<br />\nVALIDATION, not only available from <code>finding_warnings</code> on request --<br />\na caller that merely validates an otherwise-valid finding carrying one<br />\nunrecognised key gets EXACTLY ONE <code>UnrecognisedFindingFieldWarning</code><br />\nnaming that key, and no validation error. Exactly one means one<br />\nemission in total, not one per channel: an earlier revision of this<br />\nmodule ALSO logged the same text through a module logger, so a single<br />\nunrecognised key was named twice (two stderr lines). This asserts the<br />\none stdlib-<code>warnings</code> emission and that nothing anywhere in the<br />\nlogging tree logs a duplicate of it at WARNING or above.</p>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"event_loop_poli